          <div class="text-primary font-medium text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Industry · Schools · Vocational schools · Universities of applied sciences · STEM education · BTA/CTA/MTA</div>
          <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 leading-tight">Lab containers for education – school & vocational laboratories, RiSU</h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4"><strong class="text-white">Teaching laboratories to KMK RiSU 2019, pupil workstations to DGUV Information 202-058, safety cabinet DIN EN 14470, chemical fume cupboard DIN EN 14175, emergency shower and eyewash to DIN EN 15154.</strong> During GEG, fire-protection or asbestos refurbishment, chemistry, biology and physics teaching stays on plan.</p>
          <p class="text-base text-gray-400 mb-8">Refurbishment 12–24 months. Interim container laboratory in 8–12 weeks.</p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mb-8">
            <a href="#anfrage" class="bg-primary text-slate-900 font-bold px-8 py-4 rounded-lg hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 shadow-[0_0_20px_rgba(132,189,0,0.3)]">Request a school-container concept</a>
            <a href="tel:+4974357519700" class="border border-white/20 text-white font-medium px-8 py-4 rounded-lg hover:bg-white/10 transition-colors inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2">+49 7435 7519 700</a>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm text-gray-400">
            <div>✓ KMK RiSU 2019 in full</div>
            <div>✓ DGUV 202-058 for pupil workstations</div>
            <div>✓ Hire term 12–60 months</div>
            <div>✓ Take-over option after refurbishment</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Breadcrumbs bar items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/en' }, { name: 'Industries', href: '/en/industries' }, { name: 'Education' }]} />

    <AuthorBio  locale="en" />

    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/5 via-white to-primary/10 border-y border-primary/20">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <div class="text-center mb-10">
            <div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">School refurbishment backlog – container solution</div>
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Why school authorities and vocational schools choose modular containers over makeshift classrooms</h2>
            <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto">The KfW school-refurbishment backlog in DACH runs to hundreds of billions. While works proceed, teaching laboratories are missing. Improvised science rooms in office containers fail the RiSU inspection. Genuine school-laboratory containers do not.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
            <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center"><div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">8 wks</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Interim laboratory in place</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">vs. 12–24 months of refurbishment</div></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center"><div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">2.5 m²</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">per pupil workstation</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">DGUV 202-058 standard</div></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center"><div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">RiSU</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">KMK 2019-compliant</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Substance list, ventilation, protection</div></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center"><div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">RC2</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">Burglary resistance standard</div><div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">DIN EN 1627, optional RC3</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-8 text-slate-900">Standards and school rules for education containers</h2>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse bg-white rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm">
              <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-white"><tr><th class="text-left p-4 font-bold">Standard</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-bold">Application</th><th class="text-left p-4 font-bold">Delivery</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100">
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">RiSU-KMK 2019</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Safety in science teaching</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Substance list, ventilation, emergency documentation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">DGUV Info 202-058</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Science teaching – pupil workstation</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Min. 2.5 m²/pupil, demo bench, circulation</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">DGUV Info 213-850</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Safe working in laboratories</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Emergency shower DIN EN 15154, eyewash, first aid</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">GefStoffV / TRGS 526</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">School chemical storage</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Safety cabinet DIN EN 14470 F90</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">DIN EN 14175</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">School fume cupboards</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Face velocity 0.5 m/s validated, VAV-capable</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">DIN 1946-7</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Ventilation for teaching laboratories</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Min. 8 air changes with F7+F9 filters</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">DIN EN 1627 RC2</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Burglary resistance, school doors/windows</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Standard, optional RC3 for high-need sites</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">MTA Reform Act 2021 / BTA-PrüfO / CTA-PrüfO</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Vocational training BTA/CTA/MTA</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Equipment set curriculum-compliant</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="p-4 font-semibold text-slate-900">EKAS RL 6512 (CH) / BGBl. II 368/1998 (AT)</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Swiss/Austrian counterparts to RiSU</td><td class="p-4 text-gray-700">Country-specific container documentation pack</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-10 text-slate-900 text-center">Eight typical school and education containers</h2>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5">
            {[
              { title: 'Chemistry teaching lab, lower/upper secondary', desc: '24 pupils, dual demonstration, 4 fume cupboards, emergency shower, safety cabinet, preparation room.' },
              { title: 'Biology teaching laboratory', desc: 'Microscopy places, Class II microbiological safety cabinet for microbiology, BSL-1, plant climate cabinet.' },
              { title: 'Physics teaching laboratory', desc: 'Optics bench, electrical stations, mechanics set, darkened measuring niche, high voltage with safety interlock.' },
              { title: 'BTA practical laboratory', desc: 'Microbiology + clinical chemistry + haematology to BTA-PrüfO, GMP sampling.' },
              { title: 'CTA practical laboratory', desc: 'Synthesis, HPLC/GC analytics, polymer chemistry, piloting – to CTA-PrüfO.' },
              { title: 'MTA teaching module', desc: 'Clinical routine, haematology, immunohaematology, histology to the MTA Reform Act 2021.' },
              { title: 'STEM differentiation', desc: 'Electives and research clubs, coding/robotics area, maker space with 3D printing.' },
              { title: 'Interim laboratory during refurbishment', desc: 'Complete science suite for 12–36 months during GEG/fire-protection works.' }
            ].map(item => (
              <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-5 border-l-2 border-primary">
                <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">{item.title}</div>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">{item.desc}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-900 text-white">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-10">Six engineering details for school containers</h2>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
            <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6"><div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">1. Pupil safety</div><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Emergency shower, eyewash, fire alarm</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Emergency shower with heated pipework (frost protection &lt;0 °C), eyewash in every corner of the room, Category 1 fire alarm with link-out to caretaker/fire brigade, first-aid cabinet to DIN 13169.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6"><div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">2. Ventilation and fume cupboard</div><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">DIN EN 14175 school variant</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Face velocity 0.5 m/s validated, mechanical sash lock at excessive opening, school fume cupboard with demonstration viewing window, energy-saving VAV control.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6"><div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">3. Chemical cabinet</div><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">DIN EN 14470 F90 mandatory</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Safety cabinet for solvents and acids, bund, ventilation extract to atmosphere, class key system with teacher control, inventory entry.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6"><div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">4. Furniture & ergonomics</div><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Pupil furniture to DIN EN 14434</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Seat height 38–46 cm adjustable (years 5–13), bench height 64–76 cm, teacher demonstration bench with water/power/gas, abrasion-resistant surfaces.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6"><div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">5. Burglary resistance</div><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">RC2 to DIN EN 1627 as standard</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Burglar-resistant door with multi-point locking, barred windows or laminated glass P4A, motion detector linked to the school alarm, optional RC3.</p></div>
            <div class="bg-slate-800 rounded-xl p-6"><div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">6. Accessibility</div><h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">DIN 18040-1 for schools</h3><p class="text-gray-300 text-sm">Wheelchair access via ramp or lift, accessible demonstration bench (height-adjustable), minimum door width 90 cm, high-contrast signage, tactile cues.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto prose prose-slate max-w-none">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 text-slate-900">RiSU-compliant school containers: what the school authority checks</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Before the first chemistry lesson in the container, the competent school authority – in Baden-Württemberg via the government education services, in North Rhine-Westphalia via the Bezirksregierung, in Bavaria via the state school office – does not inspect the building as such, but RiSU conformity. In practice KMK RiSU 2019 requires six checkpoints: a current substance list to RiSU Annex 2 (prohibition, restriction and permission lists), ventilation evidence to RiSU §3.6 with a documented minimum air-change rate (typically 8/h to DIN 1946-7), a working emergency shower and eyewash to DIN EN 15154 with annual function test, fume cupboards to DIN EN 14175 with validated face velocity 0.5 m/s, a DIN EN 14470 F90 safety cabinet for solvents and acids, and a fire-protection report to LBO and RiSU §3.13.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">The school authority also requires a risk assessment under ArbSchG § 5 and GefStoffV § 6, which the school authority as employer prepares – we supply all technical input data (substance inventory, ventilation balance, noise forecast, fire protection). In Switzerland the cantonal school inspectorate checks to EKAS Guideline 6512; in Austria the education directorate checks to BGBl. II 368/1998. Missing RiSU documentation leads in practice to an operating ban: in 2023 several Länder shut down improvised office-container laboratories because fume cupboards were operated without validation and without an emergency shower.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">Planexus supplies a school-authority-ready pack: RiSU checklist with tick-off protocol, ventilation evidence with measurement record, fume-cupboard validation to DIN EN 14175-3, DGUV Information 202-058-compliant workstation area calculation (2.5 m²/pupil net) and a sample risk assessment as a Word template. That shortens school-authority release from a typical 8–12 weeks to 2–4 weeks.</p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 text-slate-900">Building application for temporary school laboratory containers: deadlines and documents under the LBO</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">School containers in the school yard require a building permit under LBO § 60 if gross volume exceeds 75 m³ – that applies to virtually every teaching laboratory (3–4 modules of 25–30 m² yield 225–360 m³). The accelerating route: application as a “temporary structure” under LBO §§ 65/66, time-limited to the refurbishment period (12–36 months). Required documents: 1:500 site plan with installation area, structural design to DIN EN 1991-1-3 (snow load) and 1991-1-4 (wind), fire-protection report to MBO/LBO, noise report to TA Lärm (daytime ≤55 dB(A) at the nearest dwelling), drainage evidence for fume-cupboard extract and foul water.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Permit duration varies regionally: Baden-Württemberg 6–8 weeks, Bavaria 8–10 weeks, North Rhine-Westphalia 10–14 weeks, Berlin 12–16 weeks. Container installation on school grounds additionally requires the school authority’s consent and often that of the municipal council (meeting cycle 4–8 weeks). We coordinate both procedures in parallel with factory production so that the container arrives with a valid building permit. Building-application cost including structure and fire protection: €3,500–8,000 depending on Land and number of modules – often included as a lump sum in the hire concept.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50 border-t border-gray-100">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-8 text-slate-900">Planexus services for education</h2>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <a href="/en/services/planning" class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100 hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Technical laboratory planning</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">RiSU-compliant space programming, workstation calculation to DGUV 202-058, fume-cupboard and ventilation sizing for chemistry, biology and physics teaching laboratories.</p>
            </a>
            <a href="/en/services/consulting" class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100 hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow">
